  <bioghist id="3d5e81a8153cfc87ee8feddfba44842f">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>Anthony D. Romero is a lawyer, civil rights advocate, and nonprofit executive. He worked at the Ford Foundation from 1992 to 2001 and became Director of the Peace and Social Justice Program (PSJ) Human Rights and International Cooperation (HRIC) unit in 1996. In 2001, Romero was appointed Executive Director of the American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU). He is the first Latino and openly gay man in that position.</p><p>Romero joined the Ford Foundation in 1992 as a Program Officer in the Rights and Social Justice Program (RSJ). He was appointed as Director of the newly created PSJ HRIC unit after the Foundation's program reorganization in 1996. </p><p>Prior to joining the Ford Foundation, Romero worked at the Rockefeller Foundation. He graduated from Princeton University's Woodrow Wilson School of Public and International Affairs with a B.A. in international affairs in 1987 and earned a J.D. from Stanford Law School in 1990.</p>  </bioghist>
